<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Q3 capital account surplus narrows.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Q3 capital account surplus narrows.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's third-quarter capital account surplus narrowed to $793.3 million from $1.498 billion in the second quarter, according to the central bank, the Banco de Mexico.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the account in billions of U.S. dollars:</p>
<p>						Q3		Q2</p>
<p> CAPITAL ACCOUNT			  .793	   1.498</p>
<p>   LIABILITIES			   2.781	   3.336</p>
<p>    LOANS AND DEPOSITS		-8.421	  -1.103</p>
<p>     Development banks		  .269	   -.281</p>
<p>     Commercial banks		  -.621	  -1.093</p>
<p>     Banco de Mexico		   1.254	   -.263</p>
<p>     Non-financial public	   -7.273	   -.453</p>
<p>     Non-financial private	    .458	    .987</p>
<p>    FOREIGN INVESTMENT		11.201	   4.439</p>
<p>     Direct Foreign Investment     1.479	   1.676</p>
<p>     Portfolio Foreign Investment  9.723	   2.763</p>
<p>   ASSETS				 -1.988	  -1.838</p>
<p>   ERRORS AND OMISSIONS		 .098	  -2.191</p>
<p>   CHANGE GROSS IN INT. NET RES.    .177	   -.089</p>
<p>-- Robert Kozak, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
</text>
